## Hit Math:
Accuracy = 60 + 2*Agility + weapon.AccBonus
Evasion = 10 + 2*Agility + terrain.EvasionBonus

- Added -5 to 5 randomness (Darkest Dungeon)
HitChance = Clamp(Accuracy - Evasion + context.Bonus + RNG(-5,+5), 5, 95)

Recommended caps:

Hit chance floor/ceiling: 5–95 (or 0–100 if you want harsher)
Evasion cap: ~75
Accuracy cap: ~120

## Damage Math - flat, id preserving, no runaway
- damage comes from unit baseline + weapon (plus other mods)
ex: weapon defines 4-7, might contributes flat +might bonus (small), 

RawDamageRange = WeaponDamage + MightContribution + buffs
Defender mitigation via protection (derived from vitality) w/ hard cap
	Protection = Clamp( 2*Vitality + armor + buffs, 0, 80 )
	FinalDamage = RawDamage * (1 - Protection/100)


## HP / survivability (Vitality matters, but not endlessly)

MaxHealth = BaseHp + 5*Vitality (flat per point)
Make “tanky” real, but keep time-to-kill reasonable by:
HP growth linear
PROT capped
status effects provide counterplay


## Status / control (Mind as opposed resist)

Use opposed checks like:
	ApplyChance = Clamp( BaseChance + Attacker.Mind*2 - Defender.Resist, 5, 95 )
	Defender resist derives from Mind + traits:

	Resist = 20 + 2*Mind + gear + buffs

Key DD rule: nothing is fully immune unless explicitly special. Even then, caps.
